{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1454661-looking-for-some-feedback-on-a-possible-my-guy-syndrome-situation","id":1454661,"title":"Looking for some feedback on a possible \"My Guy\" Syndrome situation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-10T15:25:41-07:00","id":1454661,"title":"Looking for some feedback on a possible \"My Guy\" Syndrome situation","content":"Ok so heres the situation, Im playing a mage who is a pop diva. She has a history of child abuse at the hands of her mother that resulted in certain flaws and what not. She has the benefactor nature and the soft hearted flaw. So she hates violence. Another character in our cabal is very angery at my characters mother for the abuse she heaped on my character during her childhood and had expressed a desire to hurt her mother. My character repeatedly asked her not to. Well the other night the cabal was at a black tie celebrity event for my character. The other character was being talked to about joining my characters security team. My characters mother crashed the event and tried to embarrass my character im a drunken rant, so the other player had her character beat up my characters mother on the red carpet in front of the press. The next day the headlines came out blaming my character for the incident as there were reports this character was part of her security team. <br /> <br /> So thats the background. Now I feel like IM in a bit of a hard place. I dont want to go and be the &quot;My Guy would&quot; person but at this point my character would cut ties with this other cabal member. She had repeatedly told her not to hurt her mom, she did it anyways and the blowback on her now is bad. Plus this kind of thing is in direct contradiction with my characters core values. But I dont want to be the asshole in the group that causes a big problem for everyone by refusing to work with the other cabal member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T17:50:08-07:00","id":1454665,"title":"","content":"I'd ask for a chance to talk to the ST and maybe just the other character's player, out of game, and see if there's a way to work out narratively for both characters to stay. It might be that you could work something out, say where your character dramatically chews the other character out and quits the cabal, only to be forced back into it by outside circumstances, that could be fun if both you and the other player are in on it even if it would feel crappy if you weren't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T18:16:29-07:00","id":1454666,"title":"","content":"This has to be hashed out out of character. If there is an &quot;asshole in the group,&quot; I would say it's the player who had their character initiate actions that clearly would be a betrayal of trust of the fellow player character the game expects her to cooperate with. But what matters isn't placing blame but addressing the problem where it stands: what does the group think about party cohesion? Is it important that the party stick together so that the focus can remain on adventures and other plot hooks, or are you one of those groups that is interested in player characters at cross purposes and the conflict that arises?<br /> <br /> If you agree that you want the party to cohere, you should brainstorm together on what sequence of events could resolve this betrayal and reconcile the characters with each other's wishes. (External devices to keep the party together, like social or circumstantial obligations, are a band-aid at best; the problem will recur somewhere down the line.) The player group from then on should keep in mind that if they want a cohesive party for their game they should have their characters arrive at compromises and understandings about any disagreements they have rather than taking hardline stances and acting against each other's wishes. You could even agree, if your players are amenable, to rewind time and play the scenario out differently, scrapping the previous version of the scene entirely. Either way, it's important that it's not just a narrative resolution, but making your fellow players mindful of the agreement.<br /> <br /> If your group decides you're interested in playing out party conflict, then as long as the players are in agreement, you can feel free to My Guy Would in good faith because you've agreed to explore where that takes play.<br /> <br /> What's important is getting everyone on the same page as to what everyone expects out of the game and what they are therefore cooperating to make happen. Don't leave it unspoken and expect everyone to accidentally land on the same expectations. Communicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T19:38:33-07:00","id":1454668,"title":"","content":"Im having discussions with the ST about this now and about how we can move forward without any disruptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T20:19:16-07:00","id":1454669,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't be &quot;with the ST,&quot; should be with everybody all together (whenever it is you're able to do that, of course). It's about getting everybody on the same page cooperatively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-11T10:01:30-07:00","id":1454693,"title":"","content":"I think it depends on the culture of the group. In many groups, discussing it with the ST or with just the ST and the other player would be at least the first step. <br /> <br /> I do agree that the original &quot;well me guy would&quot; transgression was the other player, who has their character violate your character's clearly expressed boundaries. I have trouble believing there were no other options besides assaulting someone your character had said was off limits in a way that your character had to both know about it and suffer repercussions from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24383-laughinggull","name":"LaughingGull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24383_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T07:07:29-07:00","id":1454739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LaughingGull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1454661-looking-for-some-feedback-on-a-possible-my-guy-syndrome-situation?p=1454693#post1454693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it depends on the culture of the group. In many groups, discussing it with the ST or with just the ST and the other player would be at least the first step.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the original &quot;well me guy would&quot; transgression was the other player, who has their character violate your character's clearly expressed boundaries. I have trouble believing there were no other options besides assaulting someone your character had said was off limits in a way that your character had to both know about it and suffer repercussions from it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Honestly Im starting to see this as well. She did it because &quot;she promised retribution, and she always keeps her word&quot; but other members of the cabal told her it was a bad idea and tried to stop her, my characters retainer (her manager) flat out told her that this was going to create media nightmare for her. We did play another session the cabal has come down on my side with this and now the other player is shocked shocked that my character would be angry with her for trying to protect her friend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-12T12:25:33-07:00","id":1454763,"title":"","content":"There are usually ways to resolve these things, but it depends on the group. I've RP'd with the same group for many years, so we rarely have conflicts like this anymore since we all know one another extremely well. But when there is such conflict, I agree that talking to the ST about it is a good first step, and ideally talking to the other player either alone or with the ST and/or group is a good thing. It's important to also consider that you may be able to resolve it yourself in-character - your character's first inclination might be to cut ties with the other character, but perhaps instead you hash out a plan for revenge. Or maybe events are such that your character decides that there is just no choice but to work with them - maybe they have an ability/artifact/background that is critical to your character's goals. Sometimes you do just need to fudge your initial reaction in a way that allows the game to continue, and sometimes the other guy will need to fudge their reactions for the same reason. We all do this all the time IRL too - someone at my work may have been an ass to me one time, and maybe I avoid them for a week and maybe even I secretly hate them forever, but in the end I either have to work alongside them or I need to leave the company. All of this is what tabletop RP'ing is about IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-22T17:16:05-07:00","id":1457438,"title":"","content":"Just an update. Nothing really got resolved. This player continued antagonizing not just me but eventually everyone. We reached a point where no one really wanted to interact with her, the group was increasingly leaving her out of things and she left the chronicle because she felt her character was on a different page then the rest of the group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T04:35:37-07:00","id":1457466,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a resolution to me. It would have been nice if you could have found a page everyone could have been on, but that's not always possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-23T19:55:12-07:00","id":1457540,"title":"","content":"Yeah, maybe not the best resolution but it sounds like the problem has been resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}